## The cost of exact electronic structure: what is proved (literature review, 2026-11-18)

Avik, 2026-11-18 18:46 UTC: "you're gonna trust chemists words on algos/cost? nothing here is experimental. is this combinatorial in nature?" and 20:06 UTC: "do a proper literature review this time - no faith".

1. The space is combinatorial: N electrons (N↑ up, N↓ down) on M sites occupy C(M, N↑)·C(M, N↓) configurations. For two electrons in a singlet the spatial count is M(M+1)/2.
2. Worst-case hardness is proved, not folklore. Kitaev proved 5-local Hamiltonian QMA-complete; Kempe and Regev 3-local; Kempe, Kitaev and Regev 2-local (SIAM J. Comput. 2006, quant-ph/0406180). Aharonov, Gottesman, Irani and Kempe: QMA-complete already in one dimension (arXiv 0705.4077). Schuch and Verstraete: the Hubbard model in a site-dependent magnetic field is QMA-hard, so an efficient universal density functional would solve QMA (Nature Physics 5:732, 2009; arXiv 0712.0483). O'Gorman, Irani, Whitfield and Fefferman: electronic structure in a fixed single-particle basis with fixed electron number, with no magnetic field, is QMA-complete, and the lowest-energy Slater determinant (Hartree–Fock) is NP-complete (PRX Quantum 3:020322, 2022; arXiv 2103.08215). The authors state the result is a guidepost to which structural properties reduce complexity, not a categorical roadblock.
3. Tractability is proved for structure. Hastings proved an area law for gapped 1D systems, which implies their ground states are approximated by matrix product states (J. Stat. Mech. 2007, P08024). Landau, Vazirani and Vidick gave a provably polynomial algorithm for ground states of 1D gapped local Hamiltonians, to inverse-polynomial accuracy, as an MPS of polynomial bond dimension (Nature Physics 11:566, 2015; arXiv 1307.5143). The gap is the structural property; gapless 1D remains QMA-hard.
4. The hydrogen chain (Motta et al., Simons Collaboration, PRX 10:031058, 2020) has a phase diagram with a Mott insulating phase with quasi-long-range antiferromagnetic order, dimerization, and an insulator-to-metal transition. Its insulating phases fall in the class point 3 makes tractable; its metallic phase is gapless and outside it.
5. A correction to an earlier claim: the exact ground energy of a finite Hamiltonian with rational entries is an algebraic number, a root of its characteristic polynomial, held exactly as that polynomial with an isolating interval, not in general a rational.

So for the exact model: contraction along identities can be proved to make a family tractable exactly when the family carries structure of the kind point 3 names (a gap, locality, bounded entanglement across cuts), and the proof is a bound on the quotient. No contraction makes the general fixed-basis electronic structure problem efficient unless QMA collapses (point 2).
